  "verdict": "Single-pass is a good place to start for most documents. For documents with exceptionally long or complex extractions, such as invoices or receipts with many line items, agentic extraction may do better: on [RealKIE](../idp-fundamentals/benchmark-datasets.md#realkie-fcc-verified) invoices with more than about 100 line items, single-pass got almost no line items right and agentic with Claude Haiku 5.5 got 0.44 to 0.79. Below that, single-pass scored as well or better, at about the same cost or less (agentic calls over 100,000 tokens, which Claude Haiku 5.5 bills at a higher rate, aren't priced here). Test it on your own documents.",
